A||||15||getterw||Need Help on Power Window Install||||5||
Z||000000||getterw||08-23-2001||07:43 PM||||I've got a power window/door lock 'kit' (all the harnesses, switches and motors someone took out of another Fiero).  I want to install it in my '88 coupe.  I'm keeping my old doors and installing the stuff.  However, not having seen how it came out, its a bit befuddling as to where all the wires connect and how the hardware goes in.  Does anyone have instructions or diagrams on how to do the job?<P>Thanks  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-23-2001||07:47 PM||||in my cave is some stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||08-23-2001||08:46 PM||||I'm just gonna buy new doors for mine with the stuff already in them...<P>Anybody got a set cheap?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||08-23-2001||08:59 PM||||Here is a great source of information for installing power windows/locks:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/pw_pl_install.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/pw_pl_install.htm</A>   Make sure to download the pdf that is linked at the top of the page.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||08-23-2001||09:01 PM||||Hey song man what do you mean the stuffs already in there.are you saying that these cars are somewhat pre wired for power windows even if they did not come with them from the factory?||||reg||1
Z||000005||getterw||08-23-2001||11:21 PM||||Thanks Guys.  Between the instructions from 'the cave' and the detailed diagrams and instructions from the .pdf file, I now have everything I need.  I think even a dummy like me can handle if from here.  Thanks again.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000006||Songman||08-24-2001||11:26 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by starfighter007@msn.com:<BR><B>Hey song man what do you mean the stuffs already in there.are you saying that these cars are somewhat pre wired for power windows even if they did not come with them from the factory?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>From what I have been told, your wiring harness that is in the car should already have the wiring for power accessories even if your car doesn't have it. That makes sense since they are built on a production line. <P>I'm trying to find some doors complete with everything and just be able to cut the notch in the door pillar for the wire connector to do through. I found a guy over in East TN that has complete doors for $75 each.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||mbramble||08-24-2001||12:24 PM||||My 87 coupe had none of the wiring that was required for power accessories.  I had to get the power window/lock harness and the power mirror harness from a donor and install them.  The only cars I have seen these harnesses in at the junk yard are the ones that had the power accessories.  Heck, my base coupe didn't even have wiring for floor courtesy lighting.  Had to install that harness as well.<P>All of them have, however, had the hole in the pillar already there and rubber wiring boot between the door and the pillar.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Carrolles||08-24-2001||12:40 PM||||Mbramble is right.<P>Only cars equipped with the pw/pdl have the necessary wire harness.  It is not integral with the cabin harness.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Songman||08-24-2001||01:59 PM||||Oh well.... you'd still have to find a way to splice it in even if you add the parts to your doors. Still saves a few headaches the way I see it... I doubt if I can buy just the power parts for under $75 per side.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||mbramble||08-24-2001||02:14 PM||||Dave, at Fiero Warehouse, has everything needed for adding power windows/locks for $100.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/electrical.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/electrical.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||getterw||08-24-2001||10:29 PM||||Dave, at Fiero Warehouse, is where I got all the parts I'm putting in.  That's why I didn't see how it came out of the old car.<P>The 'kit' came with everything (except instructions)--motors, switches, door locks, and the full harness; even the rubber boots for the doors.  Can't hardly beat it for a hundred bucks even if there was a tad of rust here and there.||||reg||1
Z||000012||mbramble||08-24-2001||10:51 PM||||I think that's a good price as well.  You can beat it by shopping the junkyards,  hitting deals on ebay, etc., but to get everything in a single kit is worth paying a bit extra for.  Of course you can pay a lot more than he charges as well, if you don't watch out when buying everything separately.  Seemingly low prices on individual items might not seem so low when you tally them all together.  And Dave is great to deal with.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Songman||08-25-2001||10:25 AM||||Dave = Doug<P>And yes, I recommend him on anything! He's the first person I check with when I need something...<P>Still loving my Indy I got from him!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 08-25-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000014||mbramble||08-25-2001||11:07 AM||||Yep, Doug -- not Dave.  Yesterday was a loooong day!!!||||reg||1
Z||000015||Jaxx||08-29-2001||02:01 AM||||I saw some additional info at the Fiero Online Service Guide at <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/mod.add.PW.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/mod.add.PW.html</A> <P>They had an interesting blurb about how the doors are matched to each car, making a door swap a potential nightmare. The thing that gets me is that I haven't found any pictures for reference. <P>Songman, I'd say get the complete doors if you wanted the parts and use one as a reference for installation, then take pics for the rest of us  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>------------<BR>Jaxx<BR>'86 GT work in progress||||reg||1
